{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["And the sense of <b>a land, four hundred shekels of silver</b> — according to Onkelos (Onkelos on Genesis 23:15), it means that it is worth that much. Perhaps he meant to say that its price was fixed at that amount in that place, for so is the custom in most lands, that the price of a field is set according to its measure. And according to the words of our Sages (Bava Metzia 87a), Ephron set the price at his own whim at a great premium, and Abraham, with the generosity of his heart, heard and did as he wished and increased it. And according to the plain sense, <b>a land, four hundred shekels of silver</b> — that with this Ephron or his forefathers had acquired it."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:30.193975615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}